 Fix in this order:

  1. Make clocks safe
     Easiest fix: make this a single-clock IP. Require:

  s00_axi_aclk == s00_axis_aclk == m00_axis_aclk

  Better HDL cleanup: use one aclk/aresetn internally and update IP metadata/BD
  so all AXI interfaces are associated with that same clock. If you truly need
  separate clocks, add async FIFOs between AXI-Stream and control_unit.

  2. Fix drain off-by-one
     Change:

  assign po_pp_valid_in = (state == ST_DRAIN) && (drain_wait == 0);

  to:

  assign po_pp_valid_in =
      (state == ST_DRAIN) &&
      (drain_col_cnt < pi_tile_n_size[3:0]);

  Also change ST_DRAIN so it transitions immediately when all valid columns were
  sent.

  3. Use datapath valid
     In ST_COMPUTE/ST_DRAIN, do not rely only on drain_wait >= SA_N. Use
     pi_dp_result_valid to know when output columns are actually valid. At
     minimum, gate drain start on something like:

  if (&pi_dp_result_valid) begin
      state <= ST_DRAIN;
      drain_col_cnt <= 0;
  end

  4. Limit or fix parameterization
     For now, enforce:

  SA_N = 8
  tile_m_size: 1..8
  tile_k_size: even, 2..8
  tile_n_size: 1..8

  If you want real generic support, replace hard-coded [2:0], [3:0], and SA_N/2
  assumptions with $clog2(SA_N)-based counters and ceil_div.

  5. Fix AXI-Lite write handshake
     Register writes should occur only when the write transaction is accepted,
     not just when S_AXI_WVALID is high. Use a proper slv_reg_wren signal:

  wire slv_reg_wren = axi_wready && S_AXI_WVALID && axi_awready &&
  S_AXI_AWVALID;

  Then gate register writes with slv_reg_wren.

  6. Fix test scripts
     Remove this line from both simulation Tcl scripts:

  run all

  because launch_simulation already runs the generated sim Tcl, and your
  testbench calls $finish.

  Best first patch: fix control_unit.sv off-by-one, add tile-size validation or
  documented limits, and enforce one clock in accelerator.v/IP packaging.
